# @end expo-cli

# Prebuild-generated native projects (root only — anchored with a leading slash
# so these do NOT also match local Expo modules' native source under modules/*/).
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately. Git treats `/android/` and `/android` the same
# here because android is always a directory, but EAS does not. Its project copy
# is an `fs.cp` filtered by the `ignore` npm package, which is asked about paths
# as plain strings with no way to know which are directories. A trailing-slash
# pattern therefore does not match the bare name `android`, so the directory got
# created in the copy, while every child under it matched and was skipped. The
# result was an empty `android/`, which `expo prebuild` reads as an existing but
# malformed native project: "the android project is malformed, project files will
# be cleared and reinitialized" on every single build.
/android
/ios

# Local Expo modules: ignore only their build artifacts, keep the native source.
modules/*/android/build/
modules/*/android/.gradle/
modules/*/android/.cxx/
modules/*/ios/build/

# .expo-shared
# Expo
.expo
dist/
web-build/
